# act reads this file from the working directory (and from ~/.actrc).
#
# Maps the workflow's `runs-on: ubuntu-latest` to a concrete Docker image.
# Without it, act interactively prompts you to pick a runner size on first run,
# which breaks any non-interactive use.
#
# catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest (~1.2GB) is the "medium" image: Ubuntu plus the
# tooling GitHub's hosted runners ship with (node, python, docker CLI, git...).
# GitHub's real ubuntu-latest runner is far larger (~30GB), so act's images are
# approximations -- an action that depends on a preinstalled tool GitHub has and
# this image lacks will work on GitHub and fail here. That is act's main caveat.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest